import sys; sys.path.insert(0,'..')
from con_helpers import *
save(3,8,"Two Modes of Knowing: The Mind as Bridge","Notice one moment today when the gap between you and what you are doing quietly closes, and one when it opens wide.",[
mc("U","What are the two modes of knowing in Conversation 3.8?",
 ["Difference-based knowing, which keeps a gap, and unity-based knowing, in which the gap closes.","Knowing by the senses, which is dull, and knowing by the mind, which is bright and clear.","Knowing the past, which is certain, and knowing the future, which is only a guess.","Knowing alone, which is private, and knowing with others, which is shared and open."],0,
 "Difference-based knowing, aparā vidyā, keeps a gap between knower and known and runs all of practical life. Unity-based knowing, parā vidyā, is when your inner rhythm comes into tune with what you know and there is only the thing itself.",
 "Difference-based and unity-based knowing","Part 1"),
mc("A","Two people hear the same concert. One analyses the playing; the other disappears into the music. What does Conversation 3.8 say?",
 ["Both are knowing: the first by difference, and the second by unity, as the gap closes.","Only the second is knowing, since the first has not understood a note of the music.","Only the first is knowing, since the second has lost all sense of what is happening.","Neither is knowing, since music cannot be known by a mind that is kept at a distance."],0,
 "Difference-based knowing is indispensable. The second concert-goer shows unity-based knowing: the gap closes and only the thing itself remains.",
 "Two ways of knowing the same concert","Part 1"),
judge("“The Upanishad’s teaching is that the mind is the enemy, and the path is to destroy it.”",F,
 "The old Upanishad says the mind alone is the cause of both bondage and freedom. The mind is neutral: the path is not to destroy it but to retune it.",
 "The mind is neutral: retune it, do not destroy it","Part 1"),
mc("U","What is the mind, in the picture of Conversation 3.8?",
 ["A bridge between the temporal world of parts and the whole, timeless reality, turned either way.","A wall between the inner and outer worlds, which a person has to learn to climb over.","A mirror of the world, which shows an exact copy of everything that stands before it.","A storehouse of memories, which fills up over a lifetime and is never able to be emptied."],0,
 "Turned one way, the mind steps wholeness down into separate parts that seem like the only reality; turned the other way, it lets the wholeness be recognised without losing the ability to return and act.",
 "The mind is a bridge, turned either way","Part 2"),
mc("A","A man in early practice keeps slipping away from stillness and coming back. How does Conversation 3.8 read this?",
 ["The slipping and returning is the bridge being built, and not a failure.","It shows that he is not suited to practice, so he may as well give it up.","It shows that he must try much harder, until the slipping has been stopped.","It means that he has reached the goal, since the return is the same as arrival."],0,
 "Crossing happens as the beat narrows: effortful holding, then smooth flow like oil from a jug, then the gap simply gone. The slipping and returning of early practice is the bridge being built.",
 "Slipping and returning is the bridge being built","Part 2"),
mc("U","What does the clear crystal of Yoga Sūtra 1.41 show?",
 ["A still mind goes transparent, taking the form of what rests beside it with no tint of its own.","A still mind switches off, so that nothing at all can be seen or felt by the person.","A still mind shines a light of its own, which colours everything that it looks upon.","A still mind turns hard and cold, so that nothing is able to disturb it in any way."],0,
 "The crystal glows red beside a red flower and blue beside a blue cloth. A cloudy stone cannot; only a clear one can. The mind is not empty but perfectly clear, and recognises its own nature in what it meets.",
 "The still mind is transparent, not switched off","Part 3"),
mc("A","A woman’s anxiety grabs each future thought as if it were the event. What does Conversation 3.8 suggest?",
 ["Notice, this is a thought, appearing in awareness: it loosens the grip of the thought.","Fight each thought as it arrives, since a firm stand is the way to put an end to it.","Believe each thought, since it is the mind’s way of preparing for what will come.","Wait for the thoughts to stop, and only then begin to look at what she is doing."],0,
 "Anxiety is the gap held wide and fast. Noticing that this is a thought appearing in awareness loosens it. The instrument making the symptom is the one that carries the recovery.",
 "Notice a thought as a thought, appearing in awareness","Part 4"),
mc("A","A man with rumination says, “I am so low that nothing in me is well.” What does Conversation 3.8 suggest he notice?",
 ["That he is aware of the loop, and that the awareness itself is not depressed.","That his low mood is the whole of him, so there is nothing else left to notice.","That the loop is the fault of other people, so it will end when they change.","That the loop will end if he stops looking at it for long enough and turns away."],0,
 "Depression and rumination are the beat heavy and stuck, narrowed harshly onto the self. Healing starts by noticing that one is aware of the loop, and the awareness itself is not depressed.",
 "The awareness of the loop is not itself depressed","Part 4"),
judge("“Trauma strains the bridge itself, and needs safety rebuilt slowly with skilled, trauma-informed support alongside contemplative methods.”",T,
 "Trauma swings between flooding and shutdown, so the lesson does not offer practice alone. Safety is rebuilt slowly with skilled support. The aim of recovery is fluency on the bridge.",
 "Trauma needs skilled support alongside contemplative methods","Part 4"),
mc("A","A student asks what remains distinctly human as machines take over more pattern-finding. How does Conversation 3.8 answer?",
 ["Unity-based knowing: direct recognition, creativity from stillness and compassion rooted in shared being.","Nothing, since machines will soon do every kind of knowing that a person can do.","Speed, since a person will always be able to think faster than any machine can.","Memory, since a person can store more than any machine and recall it more surely."],0,
 "Machines excel at difference-based knowing at superhuman scale, which is genuinely valuable. Unity-based knowing needs a knower that recognises itself in what is known. The danger is mistaking an imitation of the language of insight for the thing.",
 "Unity-based knowing is the distinctly human work","Part 5")])
